---
import CourseSlideLayout from '../../../layouts/CourseSlideLayout.astro';
import TirfStrategyMatrix from '../../../components/lessons/TirfStrategyMatrix.astro';
import TirfFramework from '../../../components/lessons/TirfFramework.astro';
import LessonDeckChrome from '../../../components/lessons/LessonDeckChrome.astro';
import { tirfReferences } from '../../../data/tirfSources';
import { workshopTitle, agenda, demoBrief, prompts, worksheet, cases } from '../../../data/tirfWorkshop';
import '../../../styles/tirf-workshop.css';
const title = `${workshopTitle} · April Jiawei Zhang`;
const description = 'Understand formative assessment / AfL, then use Codex or WorkBuddy to design, test and improve a language-class activity.';
const courseHref = '/teaching/training/';
const resources = '/teaching/training/tirf/resources/';
---
<CourseSlideLayout {title} {description} lessonDeck>
<section class="tirf-access" data-tirf-access aria-labelledby="tirf-access-title">
<p>AI4ELE / TIRF · 24 October 2026</p><h1 id="tirf-access-title">{workshopTitle}</h1><p>April Jiawei Zhang · City University of Macau</p>
<form data-tirf-access-form><label for="tirf-access-code">Workshop access code</label><div><input id="tirf-access-code" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" required aria-describedby="tirf-access-feedback" /><button type="submit">Open workshop</button></div><p id="tirf-access-feedback" role="status"></p></form><a href={courseHref}>Back to training</a><noscript>Enable JavaScript to use this interactive workshop.</noscript>
</section>
<div data-tirf-workshop hidden>
<LessonDeckChrome {courseHref} courseLabel="training materials" lessonTitle="AI empowered formative assessment" />
<main class="deck tirf-deck" aria-label="AI empowered formative assessment workshop">
<section class="slide is-active" data-title="Workshop outcomes" aria-hidden="false"><div class="slide-inner title-slide">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">AI4ELE / TIRF · BNBU, Zhuhai · 24 October 2026</span></header><div class="title-rule"></div>
<div data-language="en"><h1 class="cover-title">AI Empowered Formative Assessment in TESOL: <span>Designing Feedback Reflection and Learner Action</span></h1><p class="lead">1. Explain how formative assessment / assessment for learning (AfL) supports language learning.<br />2. Use Codex or WorkBuddy to design, test and improve an activity for that purpose.</p><p>Dr. April Jiawei Zhang 張家維博士<br />School of Education, City University of Macau</p></div>
<div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h1 class="cover-title">AI賦能TESOL形成性評估<span>設計回饋、反思與學習者行動</span></h1><p class="lead">一、解釋形成性評估／促進學習的評估（AfL）如何支持語言學習。<br />二、以Codex或WorkBuddy為此設計、測試及改進活動。</p><p>張家維博士 · 澳門城市大學教育學院</p></div>
<div class="actions"><button data-jump="1">Begin / 開始</button></div>
<details><summary>Workshop route / 工作坊流程</summary><ol class="agenda">{agenda.map(([en,zh,index])=><li><button data-jump={index}><span data-language="en">{en}</span><span data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden>{zh}</span></button></li>)}</ol><p>Work in pairs: one operates the tool; one checks the learning design. Swap for testing.</p></details>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="What makes assessment formative?" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Part 1: Understanding formative assessment</span></header>
<div data-language="en"><h2>What would you teach next?</h2><p>Both activities ask learners to choose the better-supported paragraph. Which evidence lets you make a better-founded decision?</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>接下來教甚麼？</h2><p>兩個活動都要求選出論據較充分的段落。哪一種證據更能支持下一步教學？</p></div>
<div class="two"><article><h3>Selection only / 只有選項</h3><p>“B. Correct. 1/1.”</p><p>You know the selection. What does this leave uncertain?</p></article><article><h3>Selection and reason / 選項與理由</h3><p>“B, because it is longer.”</p><p>The selection is the same. Would your next step be the same?</p></article></div>
<label for="opening-notice">Discuss: what do you still need to find out? / 還需了解甚麼？</label><textarea id="opening-notice" data-note="Opening observation" rows="2"></textarea>
<details><summary>Discuss first, then reveal / 討論後展開</summary><p>The learner may be using length as a proxy for support. Compare equally long relevant and irrelevant examples, discuss the difference, then ask for a fresh justification.</p><p>A mark can contribute evidence. The reason helps us choose a more specific teaching or learning next step.</p></details>
<div class="takeaway"><div data-language="en"><strong>Formative assessment / AfL:</strong> elicit and interpret evidence of learning, then use it to decide how teaching and learning should proceed towards a clear goal.</div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><strong>形成性評估／AfL：</strong>蒐集並詮釋學習證據，據此決定如何教與學，以邁向清晰目標。</div></div>
<p class="source-note">Working formulation informed by Black &amp; Wiliam (2009). Plan a fresh check of progress; the activity’s format alone does not establish formative use.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="One language goal, two criteria" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">What language learning needs attention?</span></header>
<div data-language="en"><h2>One language goal, two criteria</h2><p>Suppose intermediate English learners state opinions but struggle to support them.</p><p class="lead">Support an opinion with a specific relevant example and explain its link.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>一個目標，兩項可觀察準則</h2><p class="lead">以具體相關的例子支持觀點，並解釋兩者的聯繫。</p></div>
<div class="two"><article><h3>Criterion 1 / 準則一</h3><p>A specific example is relevant to the claim.</p></article><article><h3>Criterion 2 / 準則二</h3><p>An explanation shows how the example supports the claim.</p></article></div>
<p><strong>Task:</strong> compare two paragraphs, justify a choice, then improve the weaker paragraph. Inspect the example and explanation in the learner’s own writing.</p>
<label for="target-rewrite">Adapt this goal to a language need in your class / 按班級的語言需要調整目標</label><textarea id="target-rewrite" data-note="Learner-specific aim rewrite" rows="2" placeholder="My learners can… but need to develop…"></textarea>
<p class="takeaway">Use the same goal and criteria to judge the task, feedback and learner’s next step.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Formative practice around the goal" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Understand AfL · The design we will build</span></header>
<div data-language="en"><h2>Formative practice around the goal</h2><p>Keep the language target central as you elicit evidence, interpret it, provide feedback and support action. Select a practice to see it in our task.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>以目標為中心的形成性實踐</h2><p>蒐集證據、詮釋、回饋與行動都圍繞同一語言目標。點選各項，查看本活動如何運用。</p></div>
<details><summary>Five strategies: teacher, peer and learner roles / 五項策略：教師、同伴與學習者</summary><TirfStrategyMatrix /></details>
<TirfFramework />
<p class="takeaway">Look for what learners do with feedback, then use fresh evidence to check progress. Support may occur now or in a later lesson.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Try the learner lab" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Learner-facing demonstration</span></header>
<div data-language="en"><h2>Try the Evidence and Explanation Lab</h2><p>Choose and justify → write → use a hint and revise → explain the change → try a fresh claim.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>試用「例證與解釋實驗室」</h2><p>選擇並說明理由，找出例子與聯繫，改寫A，依提示修訂，最後解釋改動及原因。活動以英語進行。</p></div>
<div class="actions"><a class="download" href={`${resources}evidence-lab.html`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open learner lab / 開啟活動</a></div>
<p class="takeaway">With your partner, identify the evidence, feedback and learner action. Which part helps you decide what to teach next?</p>
<details><summary>Try the lab inside this slide / 在本頁試用</summary><iframe title="Evidence and Explanation Lab interactive activity" src={`${resources}evidence-lab.html`} sandbox="allow-scripts allow-downloads allow-modals" loading="lazy"></iframe></details>
<p class="source-note">Fictional examples and teacher-approved fixed hints. The lab runs locally without live AI or class response collection. Export writing inside the lab before closing it.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Codex demonstration: brief, build, test" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design with AI · Facilitator demonstration</span></header>
<div data-language="en"><h2>Codex: brief → build → test</h2><p>Watch how the same language goal becomes a working activity. You will repeat this workflow with Codex or WorkBuddy.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>Codex示範：簡報 → 製作 → 測試</h2><p>觀察同一語言目標如何成為可用活動，然後以Codex或WorkBuddy重做流程。</p></div>
<ol class="workshop-steps"><li><strong>Brief / 簡報</strong><span>Give the goal, criteria, task, hints, learner action and recheck. Review the plan.</span></li><li><strong>Build / 製作</strong><span>Ask for one HTML file in an empty workshop folder. Open the result in a browser.</span></li><li><strong>Test / 測試</strong><span>Try “B, because it is longer” and a blank response. Identify one problem, repair it and retry.</span></li></ol>
<p><strong>Watch for:</strong> when the initial attempt is captured, when hints appear, and whether the learner can revise and explain the change.</p>
<details><summary>The completed brief used in this demonstration / 示範簡報</summary><pre id="demo-brief">{demoBrief}</pre><button data-copy="demo-brief">Copy example brief</button><p class="status" role="status"></p></details>
<p class="takeaway">We choose the learning design and verify the output. The coding assistant turns the brief into a tool we can inspect and improve.</p>
<div class="actions"><button data-jump="7">Prompts used in the demonstration / 示範提示詞</button></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Pair design brief" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Plan in pairs</span></header>
<div data-language="en"><h2>Design a small activity for your classroom</h2><p>Choose one language need. Use fictional responses and agree the two criteria with your partner.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>為自己的課堂設計一個小活動</h2><p>目標需能在數分鐘內檢視。使用虛構作答，與同伴商定兩項準則。</p></div>
<div class="worksheet">{worksheet.filter(([id])=>!['difficulty','interpretation'].includes(id)).map(([id,label,placeholder])=><label for={`brief-${id}`}>{label}<textarea id={`brief-${id}`} data-brief={label} rows="2" placeholder={placeholder}></textarea></label>)}</div>
<details><summary>Diagnostic planning notes / 診斷思考</summary>{worksheet.filter(([id])=>['difficulty','interpretation'].includes(id)).map(([id,label,placeholder])=><label for={`brief-${id}`}>{label}<textarea id={`brief-${id}`} data-brief={label} rows="2" placeholder={placeholder}></textarea></label>)}</details>
<div class="actions"><button data-copy-brief>Copy my brief</button><button class="secondary" data-jump="7">Build the activity / 製作活動</button></div><p class="status" data-brief-status role="status"></p>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Build with Codex or WorkBuddy" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Your turn · Use the coding assistant</span></header>
<div data-language="en"><h2>Build with Codex or WorkBuddy</h2><ol><li>Open a new empty workshop folder in the app and start a chat.</li><li>Paste prompt 1 and your brief. Check the plan and request any changes.</li><li>Paste prompt 2 with the approved brief and your examples. Ask it to create <code>index.html</code>.</li><li>Find the generated file and open it in preview or a browser. Try the activity yourself.</li></ol></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>以Codex或WorkBuddy製作</h2><ol><li>在工具中開啟新的空白工作坊資料夾，開始對話。</li><li>貼上提示詞一及簡報，檢視計劃並提出修改。</li><li>貼上提示詞二、確認的簡報與例子，製作<code>index.html</code>。</li><li>找到生成的檔案，以預覽或瀏覽器開啟，親自試用。</li></ol></div>
{prompts.slice(0,2).map((p,i)=><details><summary>{i+1}. {p.title}</summary><pre id={`prompt-${i}`}>{p.text}</pre><button data-copy={`prompt-${i}`}>Copy prompt {i+1}</button><p class="status" role="status"></p></details>)}
<p><strong>Check before testing:</strong> can you see the goal and criteria, make an initial attempt, access a hint and revise?</p>
<details><summary>If you cannot generate a file / 無法生成檔案時</summary><p>Use the <a href={`${resources}evidence-lab.html`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">prepared lab</a> or <a href={`${resources}participant-pack.html`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">paper pack</a>. Mark how you would adapt its examples, hints and fresh task to your brief, then test that design with your partner.</p></details>
<p class="source-note">Use fictional data and the workshop folder only. This build uses fixed hints and works offline once generated; generation needs internet. Tool interfaces and access may differ.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Peer test and improve" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Your turn · Swap roles, test and repair</span></header>
<div data-language="en"><h2>Test the learning design</h2><p>Try strong, weak and blank responses. Choose the problem that most affects evidence or learner action, repair it, then repeat the affected test.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>測試學習設計</h2><p>測試充分、薄弱與空白作答。選出最影響證據或學習者行動的問題，修正後重做測試。</p></div>
<ul class="checks">{['Evidence: can a response show both criteria, rather than just the right option?','Feedback and action: do hints follow an attempt and help the learner revise?','Blank response: does the activity ask for an attempt before revealing hints?','Usability: can a learner use the controls, read long text and export the actual initial and revised writing?'].map(item=><li><label><input type="checkbox" data-check={item} />{item}</label></li>)}</ul>
<details><summary>3. {prompts[2].title}</summary><pre id="prompt-2">{prompts[2].text}</pre><button data-copy="prompt-2">Copy test prompt</button><p class="status" role="status"></p></details>
<label for="repair">Observed problem → repair → result of retest / 問題 → 修正 → 重測結果</label><textarea id="repair" data-note="Targeted repair and recheck" rows="3" placeholder="The hint appeared before an attempt → changed the reveal condition → blank input now asks for an attempt."></textarea>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Evidence to teaching action" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Teacher interpretation</span></header>
<div data-language="en"><h2>What would you do with the responses?</h2><p>A working file is ready to try. Formative use comes through the decisions we make with learner evidence. Choose a case and suggest a next step before revealing one possibility.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>同一任務，不同下一步</h2><p>選一個虛構個案，先討論初步詮釋及另一種解釋，再展開可能的行動。</p></div>
<div class="two">{cases.filter(c=>['L02','L04'].includes(c.id)).map(c=><article class="case"><h3>{c.id}</h3><p>{c.evidence}</p><details><summary>Possible interpretation, action and recheck</summary><p><strong>Hypothesis:</strong> {c.interpretation}</p><p><strong>Action:</strong> {c.action}</p><p><strong>Fresh recheck:</strong> {c.recheck}</p></details></article>)}</div>
<p class="takeaway">Evidence unclear? Check instructions or ask a diagnostic question. A clear gap? Provide focused support. Goal met? Move on or extend.</p>
<label for="case-decision">We noticed… We will… We will check again by… / 我們觀察到… 將會… 再檢視…</label><textarea id="case-decision" data-note="Evidence-to-action decision" rows="4"></textarea>
<p class="source-note">Fictional cases; interpretations are provisional. A fresh check can occur in a later task.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Two outcomes: explain and demonstrate" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Workshop outcomes · Explain and demonstrate</span></header>
<div data-language="en"><h2>Explain the purpose. Show the design.</h2><p>Show your partner the activity and one repair you tested. Then answer the two questions below.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>解釋目的，展示設計</h2><p>向同伴展示活動及已測試的一項修正，再回答以下兩題。</p></div>
<label for="exit-understanding">1. How will evidence in your activity inform a teacher or learner’s next step? / 證據如何支持教與學的下一步？</label><textarea id="exit-understanding" data-note="Exit: informing versus formative use" rows="3"></textarea>
<label for="exit-recheck">2. What did you ask Codex/WorkBuddy to build or change, and how did you check the result? / 你要求工具製作或改進甚麼？如何核對結果？</label><textarea id="exit-recheck" data-note="Exit: fresh recheck" rows="3"></textarea>
<div class="actions"><button data-export>Download my workshop notes</button><button class="secondary" data-print>Print my notes / Save PDF</button><a class="download" href={`${resources}participant-pack.html`} download>Resource pack</a><a class="download" href={`${resources}evidence-lab.html`} download>Offline lab</a></div>
<p class="status" data-export-status role="status"></p><p class="source-note">Export before refreshing or closing: workshop notes and lab writing are held separately in their open pages. Neither collects a class set across devices.</p>
<div class="actions"><button class="secondary" data-jump="11">Sources and tool setup</button><button class="secondary" data-reading aria-pressed="false">Switch to reading view</button></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Reference: sources and tool setup" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Reference · Before or after the workshop</span></header>
<div data-language="en"><h2>Sources and tool setup</h2></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>來源與工具準備</h2></div>
<details><summary>Tool setup / 工具準備</summary><p>Install and sign in before the workshop, then try creating and opening a small HTML file. Use Codex or WorkBuddy; pair up or use the prepared lab if access is unavailable.</p><p><a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/projects">Codex projects and folders</a> · <a href="https://www.workbuddy.cn/">WorkBuddy download</a> · <a href="https://cloud.tencent.com/document/product/1831/134389">WorkBuddy getting started</a> · <a href="https://cloud.tencent.com/document/product/1831/134400">Files and preview</a></p></details>

<ul class="sources">{tirfReferences.filter(r=>r.text.startsWith('Black,')||r.text.startsWith('Li,')).map(r=><li>{r.text} <a href={r.href}>Source</a></li>)}</ul>
<details><summary>Further reading and optional interpretation prompt / 延伸閱讀</summary><p><a href={`${resources}reading-list.html`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Annotated reading appendix</a></p><p>The sources provide principles and related evidence. They do not establish the effectiveness of this particular activity or either coding tool.</p><pre id="prompt-3">{prompts[3].text}</pre><button data-copy="prompt-3">Copy optional prompt</button><p class="status" role="status"></p></details>
<div class="actions"><button data-jump="0">Workshop outcomes</button><button class="secondary" data-jump="10">Notes and downloads</button><a href={courseHref}>Back to training</a></div>
</div></section>
</main></div>
<article class="tirf-record" id="workshop-record" aria-label="Printable workshop notes"></article>
<script>import '../../../scripts/tirfWorkshop';</script>
</CourseSlideLayout>
